**Item 1 — fixed.** The r2 retention wrapper in [repl.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc3/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:1484) called `jing/materialize!` inside the loader before the program ran, so a refusing store turned the round into `Error: store refused the write` and lost the value. Retention is now failure-isolated: on any throw it retains nothing and loads exactly as at master. Red-first: 45/593 with 6 failures before, 0 after; no tests re-pinned.

**Item 2 — not reproduced, no in-process path, deferred to Shiva.** The JVM peer loads zero `yin.*` namespaces (verified via `loaded-libs`) and the Node side requires only `dao.stream.*`, so the wrapper never runs on the corpus path. Measured wrapper cost is ~6 ms/round on the JVM (1368 ms vs 1175 ms for 30 rounds, store vs no-store). Locally `bb` is absent and shadow-cljs fails to load, so the Node lane is recorded as deferred-to-Shiva, not green.

